# ECOM SHARKS Constitution

## Tech Stack
- **Next.js 15** App Router, **React 19**, **TypeScript 5**
- **Tailwind CSS 4** (sole styling system), **Framer Motion 12** (animations)
- **Lucide React** (icons), **EmailJS** (contact forms), **Retell SDK** (AI calls)
- **Meta Pixel + Microsoft Clarity** (analytics), **Calendly** (scheduling)
- No database, no auth, no global state library

## Architecture Rules
- App Router only (`app/` directory) — never Pages Router
- Server Components by default; `'use client'` only when needed (state, effects, events, browser APIs)
- Components in `app/components/` (PascalCase files), utils in `app/utils/` (camelCase files)
- Route folders in kebab-case (`privacy-policy/`, `ecommerce-automation/`)
- Path alias `@/*` → project root; prefer absolute imports for cross-directory

## Performance
- LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, FID < 100ms
- Use `next/dynamic` for heavy components, `next/image` with WebP/AVIF
- Lazy-load videos via Intersection Observer
- Third-party scripts via `next/script` (`afterInteractive` / `lazyOnload`)

## Styling
- Tailwind utilities only — no CSS Modules or styled-components
- Brand: primary `#35c4dd`, darks `#063f4a` / `#052126` / `#2c2420`, light `#bef4fe`
- Fonts: Barlow + Barlow Condensed via `next/font/google`
- Custom keyframes in `app/globals.css`

## Patterns
- Functional components only, default exports, `React.memo` for expensive pure components
- Local state (`useState`/`useEffect`) — no Redux/Zustand/Context
- Shared animation variants in `app/utils/animations.ts` — reuse before creating
- API routes: `try/catch` → `NextResponse.json({ success, message }, { status })`
- Form errors: `{ type: 'success' | 'error', message }` pattern

## Security
- Never hardcode secrets; use `.env` (git-ignored), `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client vars
- Spam protection (honeypot, rate limits, content checks) on all public forms
- Security headers enforced in `next.config.ts`

## Quality Gates
- `next lint` must pass (zero errors)
- No `any` in new code
- Lighthouse perf ≥ 90 on landing pages
